            "l2kl"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2kn",
          "text": " represent injured riders and pedestrians throughout Denver and have seen how quickly a routine scooter trip can lead to serious injury, medical expenses, and complicated questions about responsibility.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2kq",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2kp",
          "text": "What the Introduction of Veo Shared Scooters Means for Rider Safety in Denver",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2kv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l2ks",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Department-of-Transportation-and-Infrastructure/Programs-Services/Transit/Micromobility-Program"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2kr",
          "text": "As Denver transitions to a single micromobility provider, city officials aim to improve oversight while reinforcing safety expectations for riders and pedestrians. According to the",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2kt",
          "text": " Denver Micromobility Program",
          "marks": [
            "l2ks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2ku",
          "text": ", scooters must operate in bike lanes or on streets, not on sidewalks, which remain reserved for people walking and using wheelchairs. Sidewalk riding is illegal, and detection technology is designed to discourage violations by slowing the vehicle or ending the ride when improper sidewalk use is detected. Operational consistency may improve under a single provider, yet safety still depends heavily on rider judgment and driver awareness in shared traffic spaces.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2kx",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2kw",
          "text": "How the Growth of Shared Scooters Has Changed Safety Risks in Denver",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2l2",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l2kz",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.denvergov.org/files/assets/public/v/1/doti/documents/programsservices/micromobility/transit/denver-selects-veo-faq.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2ky",
          "text": "As scooter use expanded across Denver, exposure to traffic conflict points increased, especially where bike lanes narrow or intersect with turning vehicles. The city explains in the",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2l0",
          "text": " Denver Selects Veo FAQ",
          "marks": [
            "l2kz"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2l1",
          "text": " that a single operator simplifies the rider and non-rider experience through a single account and app, while reducing redundant deployments and improving operational efficiency.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2l6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2l3",
          "text": "Centralized management may streamline logistics and administration, yet real-world safety still depends on roadway design, visibility, and split-second decisions made by both motorists and riders. When residents ask, ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2l4",
          "text": "“Are shared scooters safe?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2l5",
          "text": " the answer often depends on what happens at intersections and merges where different modes of transportation converge.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
