        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2n0",
          "text": "Responsibility rarely rests with a single party, and under Colorado’s modified ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2n2",
          "text": "comparative negligence",
          "marks": [
            "l2n1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2n3",
          "text": " rule, compensation may be reduced if an injured person shares fault, and recovery is barred if fault reaches 50 percent or more. Liability may involve a motor vehicle driver, a rider who ignored traffic signals, or a scooter operator whose equipment or deployment created unreasonable danger.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
